    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pappa al pomodoro is made by simmering tomatoes with garlic and oil, then stirring in torn stale bread until it melts into a thick, silky soup. It serves 4 and the key is using very ripe tomatoes or good-quality "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "passata",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "passata"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " for the best flavour."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The soup starts with an "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "aglio e olio base",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "aglio-olio"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " of garlic warmed in olive oil. This simple step builds the flavour foundation before the tomatoes go in."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
