      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Method"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "orderedList",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Warm the olive oil in a large saucepan over low heat. Add the garlic and chilli. Cook gently for 2 minutes without colouring."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the passata and stock. Stir well. Bring to a gentle simmer and cook for 15 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tear the stale bread into rough pieces and stir them into the soup. Simmer for 10 more minutes, stirring often, until the bread breaks down and the soup is thick."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Tear in the basil leaves. Season to taste. Remove from the heat and leave to rest for 5 minutes."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "listItem",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Ladle into bowls. Drizzle generously with extra virgin olive oil before serving."
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "troubleshooter",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Soup is too watery",
              "cause": "The bread needs more time to absorb the liquid",
              "fix": "Simmer for an extra 5 to 10 minutes, stirring frequently until thick"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Soup tastes acidic",
              "cause": "The tomatoes were not ripe enough or the passata was poor quality",
              "fix": "Add a small pinch of sugar and simmer for five more minutes to balance the acidity"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": "troubleshootItem",
            "attrs": {
              "symptom": "Bread lumps remain and have not softened",
              "cause": "The bread was too thick or the crust was left on",
              "fix": "Remove the crust before adding and break bread into smaller pieces"
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Where this dish lives"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pappa al pomodoro is from Tuscany, where stale bread was never thrown away. It was a cheap meal made in late summer when tomatoes were at their best. The dish became known across Italy in the 1960s. It is eaten warm or at room temperature depending on the season. You will find it in Florence and the surrounding countryside."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
